  "question": "A rectangular field is to be fenced on three sides with fixed area $A$. Find dimensions for minimum fencing and the minimum fencing in terms of $A$.",
  "answeroption": "B",
  "explanation": "Area $A=xy$.<br /><br />Wire $P=2y+x=2(A/x)+x$.<br /><br />$\\frac{dP}{dx}=-2A/x^2+1=0$ gives $x^2=2A$.<br /><br />So $x=\\sqrt{2A}$ and $y=\\sqrt{A/2}$.<br /><br />Second derivative positive, so minimum.<br /><br />Minimum fencing $=2\\sqrt{A/2}+\\sqrt{2A}$.",
  "explanation_image": [],
  "options": {
    "A": "$x=\\sqrt{A}$, $y=\\sqrt{A}$, minimum fencing $=3\\sqrt{A}$",
    "B": "$x=\\sqrt{2A}$, $y=\\sqrt{\\frac{A}{2}}$, minimum fencing $=2\\sqrt{\\frac{A}{2}}+\\sqrt{2A}$",
    "C": "$x=\\sqrt{\\frac{A}{2}}$, $y=\\sqrt{2A}$, minimum fencing $=2\\sqrt{2A}+\\sqrt{\\frac{A}{2}}$",
    "D": "$x=2\\sqrt{A}$, $y=\\frac{\\sqrt{A}}{2}$, minimum fencing $=4\\sqrt{A}$"
